WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:04.300
This is the second son of 
a mold-starter business owner,

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.480
who just started at the Agricultural 
University this spring,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.980
Sawaki Souemon Tadayasu-kun.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.550
He has the ability to see 
microbes with the naked eye.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:10.730
A. oryzae

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.490
S.   lactis  

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:12.990
A.   aceti

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.990
Amazing, isn't it?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.690
Moyashimon

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.640
I can't help it!

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.220
I have to tell someone!

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:05.250
But I haven't told Oikawa 
that I can see microbes...

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.100
Um... Um...

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.230
Horrors! The Microbe Monster

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.040
It was a microbe monster!

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.220
There were so many 
microbes covering it,

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.860
I couldn't even see a human body!

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.550
In your eyes, all humans 
should look like that.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.120
This was way different!

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.800
Where's the professor?

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.470
The professor can't help you.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.550
He went off somewhere with Yuuki.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.140
Ah, okay. I understand.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.500
Just a moment.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.030
Excuse me.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.880
Oh, Mutou-kun?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.100
It was like a giant slime mold!

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.680
There were tons of microbes that aren't

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.020
normally found on people!

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.890
If you like slime molds, 
join their little group.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.090
I don't like them...

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.730
but what are they doing?

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.640
Watching slime mold go through a maze.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.480
A maze?

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.150
Start

00:02:53.500 --> 00:03:07.970
Slime Mold (Polycephalum)

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.870
When bait is placed at the 
start and end of a maze,

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.290
slime molds grow over the 
shortest route toward it.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.210
An experiment was once conducted

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.800
on the abilities of slime molds,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.520
which have qualities of 
both unicellular and

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.970
Goal

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.000
multicellular organisms.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.500
When I told them about it, 
they wanted to see, so I started one.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:15.200
The slime mold is keeping them 
nice and quiet. I love it.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:18.510
And they've been watching 
it the whole time?

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.920
Surely slime molds don't 
move that quickly.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.010
They're showing a degree of 
concentration so wasteful, it's scary.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.780
Stupid, right?

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.390
What did the professor want?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.400
He said to have you take 
a look at this, too.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.540
What is it?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.280
Some data that a guest brought in.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.450
Proposal

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.450
Copying Prohibited

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.860
What does a big company

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.450
like this want with the professor?

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.980
Both sides benefit a great deal

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.240
when businesses and 
universities work together.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.180
The bio and environmental 
divisions of more and more

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.460
leading businesses are doing it.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.210
Hey, this is edible!

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.100
One automotive company's bio division

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.140
Really?!

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.870
even implemented 
biodegradable plastic.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.030
It's good news for you two, isn't it?

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.610
By the time you graduate,

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.640
there'll be a much wider 
range of jobs available.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.550
It doesn't really affect me.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.520
Yeah.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.140
I'll be going back home to take 
over the family business.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.150
Well, I'm sure that's fine for now.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.340
For now?

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.870
Anyway, Misato! Kawahama!

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.530
Don't you two have a debt to 
repay to your dormmates, too?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.880
Taking all their money to make

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.910
sake for the spring festival...

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.620
And then losing the sake to hiochi,

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.820
and wiping out all your 
caterpillar fungus?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.750
What are you going to do?

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.080
The spring festival is coming up soon.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.090
You didn't hear?

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.860
Professor Itsuki is 
giving us the money.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.090
Yes, I heard.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.020
You know the Hiyoshi Liquor 
Store, near campus?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.470
The professor said to buy it there.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.860
Did you really have to come, Hasegawa?

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:57.820
It's not as if I enjoy 
cleaning up your messes!

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.490
But if I gave you the money,

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.610
I suspect you'll just use 
it for yourselves again.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.840
You should trust your associates, 
Researcher Hasegawa.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.990
<i>If you call me that again, 
I will poison you.</i>

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.610
Stop instigating Hasegawa-san.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.000
<i>Associates?!</i>

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.590
Um, Hasegawa-san...

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.060
What?!

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.590
Uh, I-I just...

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:27.470
What is Professor Itsuki 
really like, anyway?

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.210
Could he have been friends 
with my grandpa in the past?

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.730
As an authority on microorganisms,

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.760
he was supposedly one of 
the people most closely

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.610
connected with the 
growth of this school.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:46.470
During the war, he was on a 
research team that made fuel

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.070
for Zero fighter planes 
using fermented potatoes.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.200
During the war? Just how old is he?

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:55.950
The professor doesn't 
talk about himself much.

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.310
It would probably be faster 
to ask your grandfather.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:05.460
Though, the reason Professor 
Itsuki took you in is simple.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.870
Any scholar would love to get his hands

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.720
on someone who can see microbes.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.250
I'm not sure how I should 
feel about that.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.430
Frankly, it's not me 
he's interested in.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.350
My ability to see microbes is 
all that matters to him, right?

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.660
Obviously!

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.700
When you judge someone, 
you judge them on their abilities.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.790
That's why people try so hard.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.310
Honestly, I despise you 
for having that ability

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.120
without even working for it.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.570
If, for example,

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:36.540
I could obtain your ability 
by drinking your blood,

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.370
I wouldn't hesitate to stab you.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.000
Of course, I'll also stab 
you if you tell anyone

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.550
about my athlete's foot.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.510
I wouldn't do that.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:50.090
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.470
So this is the professor's...

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.130
Yes, looks like this is his favorite, 
the Hiyoshi Liquor Store.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:02.070
It looks so ordinary.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:05.040
As long as I can buy liquor, 
it works for me.

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.670
Tell me when you're done ordering.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:14.900
I'll pay.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.030
Got it.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.730
Welcome.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.770
This will take care of everything 
on the list, right?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.540
Yeah.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:23.490
Kei, aren't you coming in?

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.280
Let's look around.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:28.940
Sawaki, is this place really 
the professor's favorite?

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.740
Putting all these sake bottles 
out in front of the store...

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.300
I don't know if they're on sale 
or what, but it's unbelievable!

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.150
Hey, you're right. It's lukewarm.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:42.730
Leaving sake in direct sunlight 
is basically suicidal.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.550
Sake is the most profitable item 
in all of Japan's alcohol trade.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:51.720
This is suicidal for the 
store's business, too.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.240
It's like this is how far the 
martyrdom of sake has come, huh?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.240
No, the problem here is with 
the store owner's awareness.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.060
I'm going to complain.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.080
I really appreciate you buying so much.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.820
I'll give you one free sake or shochu

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.940
for every 10 cases of beer.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.030
Are you serious?

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.420
Can you really do that?

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.420
To tell the truth,

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.840
the big brewers always give 
us a few extra bottles

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.670
free with each stock.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:18.920
We leave the stock quantities 
up to the makers,

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.960
and of course, convenience 
stores and supermarkets

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.880
sell liquor these days, too.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:26.070
It's what they call the liberalization 
of the liquor trade.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.100
Because of that, people don't even

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.200
come to liquor stores like ours anymore.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:31.690
Let them off the hook, Kei.

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.030
We don't take cards, miss.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.030
That should've been obvious...

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.410
Shut up!

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.490
I've never seen a store

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:45.750
outside of campus that 
didn't take cards!

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.140
What kind of life has she been living?

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:53.050
Also, that was the kind of card 
that only old guys carry.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:55.920
Make the receipt out to Itsuki Keizou.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.180
Oh, you're Professor Itsuki's students?

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.590
Excuse me, sir...

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.830
Hasn't Professor Itsuki 
said anything to you?

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.550
If you leave sake outside like that,

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.810
it'll go to waste in a heartbeat!

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:14.690
Grandpa!

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:16.720
Eh?

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.570
They say they're Professor 
Itsuki's students.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:34.270
Why did we have that 
sake out front again?

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.680
What? Fool!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.800
Why can't you explain it?

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.640
There's only water in those bottles.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.140
Water?

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:48.900
Yes. Just good ol' tap water.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:56.270
Th-Th-That's him! 
The microbe monster!

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.620
Th-Th-That's him! 
The microbe monster!

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.330
He's covered in microbes?

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:15.690
I have my doubts as to whether 
there's even a human in there!

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.640
All the bottles sitting out front 
are filled with tap water.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.070
Are you a fan of sake?

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:28.910
Actually, I'm the son of a brewer.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.890
Oh, is that right?

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.610
If you like, let's talk inside.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.610
Friends of Itsuki Keizou are special.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.610
W-We're going?!

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.920
It's fine.

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:42.740
You're the only one freaking out.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.890
I see!

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:55.960
You're a brewer's son, eh?

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.470
Come, come, sit wherever you like.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.210
I didn't know there 
was a bar here, too.

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:05.450
But it's sort of secluded 
for a standing bar.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:15.650
<i>The microbes are...</i>

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.490
<i>All these...</i>

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.160
<i>Who is he?</i>

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.750
Hey there, what's the matter?

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.850
N-Nothing!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.760
Do you folks smell 
anything in this room?

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.260
Now that you mention it, 
there's a sweet smell.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:52.500
It smells like melon, 
or some kind of fruit.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.590
Melon? Is it, Yuuki?

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:56.770
Yeah, it's ginjo sake.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.320
It's a miraculous fragrance 
found only in sake

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.820
that meets certain conditions.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.240
Even though it's made from rice,

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.800
ginjo sake has a sweet fragrance,

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:09.490
like ripe melon or other fruits.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.730
Sorry. It was actually a melon.

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.500
Oh. I see.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.370
Now, here is your question.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:18.760
If you know where to go,

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.160
you can buy cheap

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.700
but sweet melons directly from farmers.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:27.890
But finding good sake is not so easy.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.480
So, Sawaki, is he still 
covered in microbes?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.960
No. Most of them went 
up to the ceiling.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.140
The ceiling?

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:40.860
It's a lot like the ceiling 
at Kei's family's brewery,

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.170
and my family's cellar.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.580
The molds and yeasts 
living in this room

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.910
were clinging to the old man.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.880
They're what we call cellar yeasts.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:54.350
You mean, every time 
he leaves this room,

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.120
the microbes all go with him?

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:59.260
No way, that's impossible.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.880
You're saying the microbes love him?

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.130
A kid who can see microbes is 
in no position to deny that.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:07.880
Well, yeah, but...

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.160
Still, it seems like 
something could come of

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.290
a meeting between a 
guy who sees microbes

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.930
and a guy that microbes love.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.230
Let's think about this, Sawaki.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:21.110
The two sake freaks are soaking 
up the old man's rambling.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.210
Bored...

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:25.410
I guess it's true that you don't hear

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.360
many people say that sake is 
their favorite anymore.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:32.550
Japanese people don't think of 
Japanese sake as delicious.

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:34.750
They all love wine and beer.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.510
The very sake that Japanese 
people don't care for

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:41.750
is hailed overseas as the 
fun, exotic "Japanese sake."

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:43.570
Pardon my saying so,

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:45.110
but wouldn't the blame for that fall

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.980
on sake brewers and dealers?

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:48.150
I agree.

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.410
It is true that sake

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:52.140
has the image of being 
somewhat unapproachable.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:55.720
Only the big dealers 
and popular brewers

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:58.140
featured on TV gain any popularity.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.420
That's a given.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.540
It's the fault of the stores 
for not offering samples!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.650
The same thing happens with 
wine and shochu, doesn't it?

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.110
Sake comes with much more

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.790
label information than 
other types of alcohol.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:11.830
If alcohol dealers would properly 
explain that to customers...

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.210
And do you like sake, young lady?

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.000
I'm sorry...

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.520
I'm underage, 
so I can't quite keep up...

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:19.510
It's all right.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.530
Those who don't understand, 
don't have to.

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:23.390
It's because dealers think like that...

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:24.670
Now, don't say that.

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:29.250
In general, sake has a 
slight sweetness to it,

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.680
so people say it smells too 
much like alcohol, but...

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.690
This sake comes from a certain 
brewery in Wakayama.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.640
Care to try some?

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:46.820
Just a little.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.880
Once you've had a taste, 
give the rest to me!

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:51.450
Would you two like to try it, too?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.700
Yes!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.130
Hey, now.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:58.480
You're underage. Just leave this to me,

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.330
and find some way we 
can use the old man.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:05.040
Like discovering a new species 
among the microbes on him?

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.510
Wait a minute! Can you really do that?!

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:09.630
How is it?

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.470
Oh, I'll try it now.

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:16.050
It's delicious...

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.070
Is this really sake?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.480
The chief of a brewing cellar,

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.230
who's also an agricultural 
university alumni,

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:25.020
makes this sake by himself.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.810
It's unprocessed daiginjo 
sake made with mineral water

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:29.740
from a spring designated as a World

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.410
Heritage site in Wakayama.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.380
Limited Edition

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:36.320
Not much is produced, so you 
won't find it just anywhere.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:38.680
For unprocessed daiginjo,

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.980
it's a real bargain at 5000 yen.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:44.160
I see what you mean. 
It's not just the smell.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.670
It tastes almost like fruit, too.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:48.670
It's the only sort of alchemy 
that man has succeeded in.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.900
What we call sake, is a miracle

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:54.700
produced through fermentation 
by the power of microbes.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.240
Oh, Itsuki-san!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.010
Wh-When did you get here?

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:04.020
What do you think, Yuuki-kun?

00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:13.270
You're right. Just from the smell,

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:15.300
I can tell that it's been 
made with great care.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:20.700
Does it have something to do with the

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.210
microbes all over the old man?

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.620
We did our best!

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:25.420
No, I don't think they have 
anything to do with it.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.210
It's just good sake from the start.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:30.190
Maybe a liquor store owner 
shouldn't say this,

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.410
but it's true that there 
are so many types of sake,

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.350
it's hard to choose among them.

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:38.970
Frankly, people make the 
wrong choices all the time.

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.940
But that's why we're so happy

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:43.560
when we encounter a good one.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.600
There's still lots of good sake

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:48.470
somewhere out there, just like this one.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:52.830
You all should look for the 
sake you like best, too.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.480
Welco—

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:56.190
Of course, there are 
some who believe

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:58.080
it's quicker to just make their own.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.790
I would personally 
recommend that route.

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:08.030
So... is this a place used for 
letting people sample good sake?

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.810
Everything out in the store 
looked relatively normal.

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:15.120
But more significantly, 
this room has no entrance.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.050
It almost looks like a speakeasy.

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:19.880
You tell people to look for 
good sake on their own,

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.740
yet the bottles out front 
only have water in them.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:26.190
Something tells me there's more 
to this shop than meets the eye.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:28.340
Grandpa!

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:31.190
There's a woman out front demanding 
to see Professor Itsuki!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.850
Oh, then I'll come out there.

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:37.640
Yes, I'd rather not show this 
place to any more outsiders.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:38.450
Hey, don't come in here!

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:41.000
Professor!

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:41.910
Hey!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:46.100
You told me on the phone to 
meet you outside the store!

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.370
That stinks!

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.370
It won't last much longer!

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.020
I've got to get everything in

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.020
Wh-Who is that?

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.340
That's Mutou,

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.240
my backpack into a refrigerator, now!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.880
our lab's one and only seminar student.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.840
Come on, lady, 
you have to wait outside!

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.130
You idiot!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.760
Don't jostle the backpack!

00:17:59.080 --> 00:17:59.930
What the—

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:06.400
Welcome back, Mutou-kun.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.110
Her backpack exploded.

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:16.780
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:19.880
Sorry my student made 
such a mess, Kikuji-san.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:21.520
It's no big deal.

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:24.240
Despite appearances, 
my grandson loves to clean.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.530
It's the professor's fault.

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:29.330
I asked him on the phone 
for immediate action.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.130
Don't be so childish!

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.050
By the way,

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.130
are you the Sawaki-kun that 
Itsuki-san told me about?

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:38.880
Y-Yes...

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.110
Show the microbes some love.

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:46.280
Without their powers, 
we wouldn't be able to do anything.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:06.840
I really do want to give you 
a welcome back hug, you know.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:08.050
Don't worry about it.

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:10.160
I'm aware that I stink.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.860
<i>I never did get a chance 
to find out why</i>

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.380
<i>the microbes were clinging to him.</i>

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:17.340
Obviously!

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:22.140
When you judge someone, 
you judge them on their abilities.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.010
That's why people try so hard.

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:26.990
Honestly, I despise you for having

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:28.850
that ability without even working for it.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.020
<i>Even if you tell me that, 
my ability is just...</i>

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.250
Show the microbes some love.

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:39.780
Without their powers, 
we wouldn't be able to do anything.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.450
Tadayasu!

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.660
<i>Love the microbes?</i>

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:53.090
Gross...

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:56.550
Man, that woman totally reeked.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.910
I wonder if I can get rid of 
the stench by this evening.

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.860
What a great smell!

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.550
Love it!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.340
Moyashimon

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.340
Episode 5

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.340
Microbe Theater

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.340
Microbe Theater 5!

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:28.990
What's that?

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.780
Wow!

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:34.540
Who are you guys?

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:36.780
We're cerevisiae.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.580
Cerevisiae

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.980
Humans call us yeasts.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:44.580
We turn the sugar, that you 
oryzae make, into alcohol.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:51.120
Sugar

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.770
Convert starch to sugar!

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.590
Convert starch to sugar!

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:50.520
I ate sugar and it came out as alcohol!

00:21:51.380 --> 00:21:53.090
Wow!

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:56.540
And who are the girls with the 
numbers on their foreheads?

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:59.760
Well, you can find microbes anywhere,

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.540
but these girls come 
from pure cultures.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.050
They've had very sheltered lives.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:05.630
They're managed by humans.

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:06.130
6

00:22:06.310 --> 00:22:08.630
I make light, mild sake.

00:22:09.150 --> 00:22:11.640
I make strong sake.

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:14.640
I can ferment even in low temperatures.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:17.640
I'm made for daiginjo sake.

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:21.560
Kyokai Yeasts

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:24.820
Sheltered girls sure are different...

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:29.820
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 6,

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:29.820
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:29.820
Asia's Top Five Food Poisoning Microbes

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:38.870
Next Week: 
"Enchanting! Miss Agricultural University"

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:34.000
Mutou-kun, did you see a UFO?
